<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Roque Dalton</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1935">1935</a>–<a href="/years/1975">1975</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Roque Dalton was a Salvadoran poet, essayist and revolutionary, regarded as one of the most important <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/latin">Latin</a> American poets of his generation. Imprisoned and exiled for his political activity, he spent years in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mexico">Mexico</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cuba">Cuba</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/prague">Prague</a>, and his works include Poemas clandestinos. He joined the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/guerrilla-warfare">guerrilla</a> People's Revolutionary Army and was killed in 1975 by members of his own organisation.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/roque-dalton.jpg" alt="Roque Dalton" width="320" height="205" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Casa de las Américas · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Roque_Dalton_(1969).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
